{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Take, please.</b> Meaning: immediately and at once, without asking for time — and this too is part of the trial, that he not ask him for time, as in the case of the daughter of Jephthah (Judges 11:37), whose father wished to offer her as a burnt offering and she asked him for two months, etc." "<b>Further,</b> He hinted to him that he should take Sarah with words, to persuade her to agree to go with him. And so they said, of blessed memory (Tanhuma 22), that all that night Abraham was placating Sarah to agree with him to let him take him to learn Torah until the light of morning." "<b>Further,</b> it alludes concerning Isaac, that he should take him with words of favor — for he had never been tested all his days — and HaShem commanded that he take him with reasoned words and instill in his heart the merit of the matter, if he would offer a burnt offering to HaShem." "<b>Your son, etc.</b> Here is an allusion to the three loves that the Torah obligated every Jew to love the Creator, blessed be He, with all heart and with all soul and with all might (Deuteronomy 6:5). 'With all heart' — there is nothing dearer in a person's heart than love for his children, and that is His saying <b>your son.</b> And corresponding to 'with all your soul' He said <b>your only one</b> — and since he has none but him, he is his very soul, for one who has no children is considered as dead. And corresponding to 'and with all your might' He said <b>whom you love</b> — meaning: him you loved more than all your possessions, and all his possessions are as nothing compared to him; yet even so, 'offer him up to Me,' etc. And HaShem intended to spell out all this in order to inform him that even though he holds these at every level of intensity, even so HaShem desires that he offer him to Him as a burnt offering."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:44.860544555Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}